<article class="env-definition" id="0AAH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AAH">Definition <span data-tag="0AAH">10.103.12</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $M$ be a finite $R$-module. We say $M$ is <em>Cohen-Macaulay</em> if $M_\mathfrak p$ is a Cohen-Macaulay module over $R_\mathfrak p$ for all primes $\mathfrak p$ of $R$. </p>
